title: 'fix(babe): make BABE aware of duplicated authorities'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    An authority listed more than once in the BABE authority set now has the summed weight of all its
    entries when its primary slot threshold is calculated. This matches how GRANDPA's `VoterSet` and
    BEEFY's `RoundTracker` (https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/pull/8964) handle duplicated
    authorities.

    The BABE VRF output depends only on the authority key, the slot, the epoch index and the epoch
    randomness, not on the authority's index. A key listed `k` times therefore had a single primary
    draw at the threshold of one entry, while secondary slot assignment counts every entry.
    With the summed weight, its primary threshold is `1 - (1 - c)^(k/n)`, the same as `k` independent
    entries.

    Authority sets without duplicates are unaffected.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `sp_consensus_babe::check_equivocation_proof` no longer requires both headers to carry the same
    authority index. Both seals are still verified against the offender's key. An authority listed
    more than once could otherwise equivocate under two of its entries without a valid proof.
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    On chains whose BABE authority set contains duplicated keys, nodes with this change accept primary
    blocks that nodes without it reject. All block producers and importers of such a chain must
    upgrade together.
crates:
- name: sc-consensus-babe
  bump: patch
- name: sp-consensus-babe
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-babe
  bump: none
